From 8ed3f577620b8f5b5ccf42cc87a77aa36de39c73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 02:23:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] test: Provide the local runtime capabilities required by MCP
 fixtures

Host Python stdio servers require an explicitly registered local environment
and an existing host cwd when the primary executor lives in a container.
Keep the remote primary, route each fixture through existing mixed-environment
support, and use the test-owned Codex home for local stdio startup. Enable the
upstream code-mode host for the yielded-cell fixture rather than silently
falling back to direct tools.

Base: rust-v0.163.0 (83086188ae0614bd882818ff1aa23f3194962012).
Integrated local verification: 49 focused tests pass without retries.
The prior yielded-cell fixture returned unsupported custom tool call: exec.
Standalone and remote Docker verification are recorded separately.
